  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PIP:Youth Empowerment for Resilient Communities in Tajikistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through targeted interventions, the project aims to support the meaningful participation of young people in local development processes andthe implementation of social initiatives by youth-led volunteer organizations to contribute to social cohesion and resilience at the local level.The trained young women and men are expected to become more resilient, have a positive impact on society, and engage in dialoguebetween with the local authorities on issues affecting young peoples lives. Additionally, the project will leverage the PVE Toolkit developedunder the STRIVE Asia project to strengthen the capacities of national and local authorities, community leaders, women activists, and religiousleaders for meaningful implementation of youth-focused policies at the local level and integrate youth priorities into District DevelopmentPlans.</narrative>
  </description>
